" Vertical tab bar toggle (<Space>b)
" Each command applies its theme and then rebinds <Space>b to the other one,
" so a single key flips back and forth.
command! sidebarhide <:colorscheme vertical_tabs_hidden><:nmap <Space>b <:sidebarshow>>
command! sidebarshow <:colorscheme vertical_tabs_custom><:nmap <Space>b <:sidebarhide>>
nmap <Space>b <:sidebarhide>

" Tab marking (<Space>e)
" Toggles a highlight background on the CURRENT tab, for grouping tabs
" visually. Vieb 12.6 has no per-tab colour/label feature, so this rides on
" the per-tab `muted` flag -- the only toggleable per-tab state that leaves
" tab order and page state alone.
" TRADE-OFF: a marked tab has its audio muted. Press <Space>e again to
" unmark and unmute. The colour is --tab-marked-bg in the colorschemes.
" PERSISTENCE: the mark lasts as long as the tab does. :mute writes it to
" disk, so it also survives a restart for any tab that is itself restored --
" with restoretabs=pinned above, that means pinned tabs only.
nmap <Space>e <:mute>

